+factors of its right-angled Artin group and computes them as components of the
+complement graph.  Section 6.3.1 uses those factor counts as values of a monic
+polynomial; its constant term is the secret.
+
+Generation is inverse.  It chooses small factor counts first, interpolates the
+unique monic polynomial implicitly, and realizes every count as the number of
+orbits of an exact cyclic noncommutation rule.  No generated instance is solved
+to obtain its planted certificate.
