codex
The paper supports the existing family: Sections 4 and 6.3.1 explicitly connect maximal join factors, complement components, and the polynomial secret-sharing value. It must be Track B—Proposition 4.2 is a polynomial-time component algorithm. I found one compliance bug in the current draft: its G9 result still gates on the hinted oracle, although today’s contract gates only answer size and intended-route cost. I’m auditing the rest before patching and rerunning.
