codex
The solved transcripts exposed the weak point: the old generator made almost every factor count identical, reducing interpolation to a handful of corrections. I’ve kept the same Section 6.3.1 family but now draw every shipping count from the same four-value alphabet and conjugate each cyclic complement by an independent exact Feistel relabelling. The witness remains inverse-generated; the compact route is 125–175 operations across the named presets, while literal graph processing now includes millions of Feistel-round evaluations.
exec
/bin/bash -lc 'python3 gen_1802_04870.py' in /home/gson/gvrepo/results/1802.04870
