codex
Implemented a self-contained `TRACK = "B"` generator based on the paper’s Section 6.3.1 secret-sharing scheme and Proposition 4.2 decomposition algorithm ([paper PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1802.04870)).

Deliverables:

- [gen_1802_04870.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1802.04870/gen_1802_04870.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1802.04870/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1802.04870/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1802.04870/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1802.04870/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1802.04870/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Exact random-guess probability: approximately `2.06e-19`; sampled `0/200,000`.
- Four attacks: `0/8` successes each.
- Reference algorithm: `23,592,960` counted operations across eight instances, solving `8/8`.
- Compact route: at most `127` exact operations.
- Answer size: 23 characters and 2 atoms.
- JSON emission and 20-instance canonical diversity dry run passed.

The result is not yet STEP-4 shippable: OpenRouter exhausted its total key limit, so all three final oracle arms recorded four HTTP 403 errors and zero scored attempts. The provisional `easy` shipping preset must be rerun once quota is restored; no hardness verdict was fabricated.
